---
// ============================================================
// /now/ — what he is working on at the moment.
//
// A "now page" is a short, dated statement of current focus. The
// date is the point: an undated one silently becomes a lie.
//
// To update it, change the text and the date below. That is the
// whole maintenance burden.
// ============================================================

import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// Change this whenever the page is updated.
const lastUpdated = new Date("2026-09-11");

const formatted = new Intl.DateTimeFormat("en-GB", {
  day: "numeric",
  month: "long",
  year: "numeric",
  timeZone: "UTC",
}).format(lastUpdated);

const iso = lastUpdated.toISOString().slice(0, 10);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Now"
  description="What Anupam Kumar is working on at the moment."
>
  <article class="prose" data-pagefind-body>
    <h1>Now</h1>

    <p class="updated">
      Last updated <time datetime={iso}>{formatted}</time>
    </p>

    <p>
      This site has just gone up. What exists so far is the structure: the
      writing, the shape of the data layer, and the rules the whole thing is
      built to.
    </p>

    <h2>Working on</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>The first essays.</li>
      <li>
        Choosing the first three datasets to clean and publish. The test is that
        the raw source should be public but painful to use, because that gap is
        where the work is worth doing.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Next</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>
        A browsable data section, generated from each dataset's own metadata
        rather than a list kept by hand.
      </li>
      <li>
        The first two tools — one small and rule-based, one that genuinely needs
        a wide screen — built together so the plug-in design is proved rather
        than assumed.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="explainer">
      This is a <a href="https://nownownow.com/about">now page</a>: a short,
      dated statement of what has my attention, rather than a list of everything
      I have ever done.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .updated {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--colour-ink-muted);
  }

  .explainer {
    margin-top: var(--space-7);
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--colour-rule);
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    color: var(--colour-ink-muted);
  }
</style>
